Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patches 0001-0021 + 0023-0034 (touches
spec_decode/dspark/speculator.py only). VLLM_DSPARK_CONF_HEAD=<head.npz> (default unset): the DSpark speculator reads
its per-position draft confidences from a head fitted to this target's own acceptance (fitted offline,
from a fixed:k round log with patch 0034's confidence inputs) instead of the checkpoint's one Linear(5,376 -> 1): per
draft position i, sigmoid(x . w[i] + b[i]) over the same x = [the drafter's hidden at the sampled position, the Markov
embedding of the previous token] in fp32, plus, with w1 / b1 / w2 / b2 in the file, a residual MLP
w2[i] . gelu(w1[i] x + b1[i]) + b2[i]. Only the verify depth (patch 0010's conf rule) reads the confidences, and rows
up to any depth compute what the full window computes for them, so greedy text does not change; the drafts do not move
either. Why: on our panel the checkpoint's head separates accepted from rejected drafts at AUC 0.83 / 0.82 on writing /
chat (0.90 on code), and a replay of the depth rule with a sharper predictor is worth up to +6% on those domains
(Oct 21). Test: patches/tests/test_dspark_conf_head.py (serve image).

